# Kumano Faces Kakkazan chapter III (turn 5) exiles the Saga and returns it transformed as Etching of Kumano, a 2/2 haste
# Enchantment Creature (CR 712.14a). Its replacement exiles a creature that dies after a source its controller controlled
# dealt it damage THIS turn (CR 614.1a, 700.4): Bot1's Lightning Bolt kills Bot2's Ornithopter on turn 5 -> exiled. Not
# when the damage was dealt on an earlier turn: Spellskite was Bolted for 3 on turn 3 (it has 4 toughness and survives),
# and destroyed by Cut Down (no damage) on turn 9 -> graveyard. Not when the damaging source was Bot2's: on turn 6 Bot2's
# own Lightning Bolt kills its other Ornithopter -> graveyard. Only a creature is exiled: Bot1's Bolt also kills Bot2's
# Wrenn and Six (3 loyalty) on turn 5, which goes to the graveyard. Only a creature that dies: Bot2's second Spellskite is
# Bolted for 3 on turn 7 and then returned to hand by Unsummon, not exiled.

